.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt RACH2 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rach2
.Nd an educational operating system for the 32-bit PC
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Rach2 is a kernel and a small userland for the 32-bit x86 PC, written to be
read.
The kernel is freestanding C89; the userland is the ported musl C library,
the BusyBox shell and tools, the Dropbear SSH server, the TinyCC compiler
and the pdpmake
.Xr make 1 ,
so the system can rebuild its own kernel.
.Pp
The system boots from a KRFFS image in memory or from an ext2 root on a
disk, mounts FAT32, exFAT, ext2 and KRFFS volumes, drives ATA and AHCI
disks, USB keyboards and sticks, and RTL8139, e1000 and RTL8168 network
cards, and answers SSH.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/share/man
.It Pa /usr/share/man
The manual pages, as plain text under
.Pa catN .
.It Pa /src
The kernel, shell and utility sources, on the images that carry a compiler.
.It Pa /proc
The kernel's counters and tables, one file each.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr man 1 ,
.Xr sh 1
.Sh HISTORY
Rach2 is developed as a teaching system; its milestones are recorded in the
source tree under
.Pa dev-log .
